course: dictionary
lesson: 5284
title: July and the calendar
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: July is a month, the seventh one of the year. Its name is written with a capital letter, like all month names. When you read «in July» or «early July», the word tells you the time of year. Look at the words around it to find out more.
explain: July has 31 days. That is one more day than June, which has 30. In maths problems you can add the days of two months: June and July together have 30 + 31 = 61 days.
explain: Where you live changes what July feels like. «France is in the northern half of the world, so July is summer and Christmas is in winter there.» In Australia and New Zealand it is the other way round. There, July is winter, so the context clue tells you which half of the world the text is about.
fact: July is the seventh month of the year.
fact: July has 31 days.
fact: In the northern half of the world (USA, UK, Canada, Ireland) July is summer, and it is often the summer holidays.
fact: In Australia and New Zealand, July is winter.
fact: «14 July 1789» is a date in Paris, France, when people took the Bastille, a prison fortress.
exercise: «France is in the northern half of the world, so July is summer there.» What season is July in France? | *Summer | Spring | Winter | Autumn
exercise: How many days does July have? | 29 | 28 | *31 | 30
exercise: Which word names the seventh month of the year? | August | June | *July | May
test: In Australia and New Zealand, what season is July? | Autumn | Spring | Summer | *Winter
test: June has 30 days and July has 31 days. How many days are there in June and July together? | 60 | 62 | *61 | 59
exam: Mia says July is always summer. What is the best answer? | It is winter everywhere in the world | July has only 28 days, so it is short | *It is summer in the north, but winter in Australia and New Zealand | It is summer everywhere in the world
